We've been together for over 3 years (don't yet live together). He has great earning potential. He often makes amazing money, but he's terrible at "adulting". He doesn't save a cent, he's often in debt, behind on bills...that type of thing. He also struggles with just life in general (ex: he only eats via UberEats, he refuses to drive so he takes cabs everywhere, he doesn't do anything that's domestic so if he doesn't have a current cleaning lady...as is the case at the moment...his house is a mess and covered in SO MUCH FUR because he also has 2 dogs). He is between contracts right now (he usually can easily pick up contracts and he makes a lot of money on them) so he's stretching his last paycheck over Christmas.

&amp;#x200B;

I did live with him during the pandemic, but I found it difficult because I was expected to look after all the adulting. His cleaning lady didn't work during the pandemic so I was doing the cleaning and cooking, and he was kind of depressed and staying in bed until dinnertime. We'd eat dinner, I'd clean up, then he'd want to play cards until midnight. I went along with this because he was depressed, but that routine + allergies to the dogs (and every day I was sweeping up so much fur) and I went back to my own apartment when the lockdown lifted.

&amp;#x200B;

We had a falling out at the beginning of the month and didn't talk for 3 weeks. However we worked things out, so we will be spending Christmas together. The latest issue that is bothering me:  he doesn't have a cleaning lady at the moment, so his place is once again a mess and covered in fur. He tells me he can't deal with finding a new one and asks me to find one for him. Well each one I find is an issue....the main issues are he feels they are charging too much or that they want to do an initial walk-through. Then the 2nd issue is that he didn't get a Christmas tree. So here we are, 6 days before Christmas and he's telling me he NEEDS a tree. And he is asking me to "help". I tell him we can order a fake tree off Amazon for next day delivery. No...he only wants a real tree. So I find someone who can deliver a tree. He thinks he's charging too much but agrees to pay it. The guy can only deliver it on Wednesday during a certain time. He says he won't be here because he has an appointment.

&amp;#x200B;

This kind of thing I've dealt with our entire relationship and it's really driving me bonkers lately. He seems illogical. His house is covered in fur. Who wants a real tree in the middle of all that? It's going to be more expensive than necessary. And he'll only get it days before Christmas (and he's going to his dad's for Christmas anyway). And on top of everything else, it MUST be real. And he can't "adult" to make this happen so he needs my "help".

&amp;#x200B;

This type of thing has happened repeatedly with so many issues (landscaping, snow removal, dog walkers, bookkeeping, etc). I HATE it. For some reason, nothing is ever easy with him.

&amp;#x200B;

I just want a calm, stress-free life. My own place is clean. I don't make a lot of money, but I don't spend recklessly so I don't NEED a lot of money. I have my own place decorated for Christmas (for a few weeks now). And my tree is small, pre-lit and white lol. I love him, but I feel like he's always doing weird things to make life more stressful than it needs to be. I have no idea what I can even say to him to deal with this effectively? Or if it's just hopeless and we should go our separate ways. Help please!

&amp;#x200B;

